{
 "version": 1,
 "title": "Random Step Lead",
 "category": "Leads and stabs",
 "text": "Sound: a nervous, computer-generated melody: hold one key and it plays a random tune around it, a new note every eighth, stepping from one to the next.\n\nHow it's built: a Clock's 1/8 triggers a Sample & Hold, which takes a new random value each time (from its own noise); that goes into the oscillator's FM (half an octave either way), so the pitch steps randomly around the key you hold. The steps are hard (no glide); a filter envelope, retriggered by the same clock, plucks each one. Delay for echoes. One voice.\n\nPlay: hold a key; change keys to move the tune.\n\nTweak: the oscillator's FM (how far the notes wander), the clock's TEMPO and output, the delay's FEEDBACK. Put a Slew between the Sample & Hold and FM for glides.",
